sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Ed as Editor / marketer
  participant UI as Web UI (or CLI)
  participant API as FastAPI
  participant EN as promo_engine
  participant LLM as LLM (optional)

  Ed->>UI: Drop folder / zip of 50 screenplays (+ manual promos CSV)
  UI->>API: POST /api/jobs (files, options)
  API->>EN: run_pipeline()
  EN->>EN: Read every file, split episodes, parse timed beats
  EN->>EN: Score every beat (hook, cliffhanger, intensity, context)
  EN->>EN: Score every 20–60 s window that starts/ends on a beat
  opt LLM_API_KEY set
    EN->>LLM: Top 30 candidates as numbered lines (5 per call)
    LLM-->>EN: Scores, hook / cliffhanger / why, tighter L# bounds
    EN->>EN: Validate edits against real beats, blend 50/50 with rules
  end
  EN->>EN: Diverse top-K, posting order, quality flags
  EN->>EN: Match against manual promos (IoU), diagnose each miss
  EN-->>API: Run result (promos, transcripts, metrics, comparison)
  API-->>UI: Job done (UI polls progress meanwhile)
  Ed->>UI: Review ranked list, phone preview, keep / reject
  UI->>API: POST /api/feedback (stored for `promo-finder learn`)
  Ed->>UI: Export cut sheet / EDL
  UI->>API: POST /api/export/edl (stateless)
  API-->>Ed: promos.edl → Premiere / Resolve timeline
  Note over Ed,EN: An editor's day of watching becomes ~1 s of compute plus a review of the top 10.
